{"step_index":78,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-26T03:22:11Z","input_tokens":243,"cache_read_tokens":67456,"output_tokens":721,"content":"**\"Contribution by Contributor\"** is mounted — 8 lines, 83 days, same noise filters.\n\n## Per-Contributor Totals (sum of daily contribution levels)\n\n| Rank | Contributor | Total | Share |\n|:--:|---|---:|---:|\n| 1 | Maxime Beauchemin | 532.2 | 36.0% |\n| 2 | Kamil Gabryjelski | 276.8 | 18.7% |\n| 3 | Richard Fogaca Nienkotter | 233.3 | 15.8% |\n| 4 | Kasia | 146.1 | 9.9% |\n| 5 | Amin Ghadersohi | 101.4 | 6.9% |\n| 6 | Evan Rusackas | 78.7 | 5.3% |\n| 7 | Antonio Rivero | 70.6 | 4.8% |\n| 8 | Türker Ziya Ercin | 30.2 | 2.0% |\n\n## What the Per-Author View Reveals\n\n**1. It's not a one-person repo — but it is top-heavy.** Maxime leads at 36%, yet the top 4 together cover ~80%. That's a tight core, not a solo project.\n\n**2. Each person has a distinct cadence:**\n- **Maxime** — near-continuous, rarely a zero day. The steady baseline.\n- **Kamil** — bursty. Silence for stretches, then high-value spikes: 10.99 (Aug 20), 10.18 (Aug 26), 10.15 (Sep 8).\n- **Richard** — the most *consistent mid-tier* contributor; almost never spikes above 9 but almost always present when active.\n- **Kasia** — concentrated in UI work; strong late-Oct surge (7.82, 7.85, 8.05 on Oct 12–14).\n- **Amin** — smallest footprint but efficient: 6–7 per active day on few commits, i.e. large focused changes.\n- **Türker** — only 4 active days total (Jul 28, Aug 9, Aug 11, Aug 14, Aug 17, Sep 23) — very low volume.\n\n**3. Oct 8 is the collaboration highlight** — 7 of 8 contributors active in one day, and Kamil (9.38) slightly edged out Maxime (8.38). That's the single most distributed day in the window.\n\n**4. The Aug 2–Aug 30 stretch is Maxime-dominated**, with occasional pairings (Maxime + Richard on Aug 6–8). Then **September onward becomes visibly more multi-author** — the team's collaboration widened over the quarter.\n\n## Two Caveats\n\n- **Additivity:** as flagged, per-author levels don't sum to the aggregate chart's value (log2 isn't additive). The aggregate shows *total activity*; this chart shows *allocation across people*.\n- **Tagging accuracy:** attribution follows git author, so pairing/squash-merges credit the committer. If the team uses squash-merge, one person may get credit for a collaboratively-built PR.\n\nWant me to add a **stacked area** version (shows share-over-time cleanly) or an **author filter dropdown** to let you isolate one person?"}
